WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.890
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:10.990
Today we are going to spice up this family
video with a new, stylized environment.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:18.770
Then, we make a video of a boat trip much
more memorable, up the authenticity of a parkour

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:29.730
video, decorate a swan, enhance our clothing
a little, and conveniently forget about a

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.780
speeding motorcycle.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.079
Only for scientific purposes, of course.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:39.820
So, these are all very challenging tasks to
perform, and of course, none of these should

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.120
be possible.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.440
And this is a new AI-based solution that can
pull of all of these!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.440
But…

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.440
how?

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.870
Well, in goes an input video, and this AI
decomposes it into a foreground and background,

00:00:53.870 --> 00:01:02.220
but in a way that it understands that this
is just a 2D video that represents a 3D world.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:08.049
Clearly, humans understand this, but does
Adobe’s new AI do it too?

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:11.219
And I wonder how much it understands about
that?

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:14.049
Well, let’s give it a try together.

00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:18.179
Put those flowers on that dress, and…what?

00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:23.590
The flowers look like they are really there
as they wrinkle as the dress wrinkles, and

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.939
it catches shadows just as the dress catches
shadows too.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:30.359
That is absolutely incredible.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:35.979
It supports these high-frequency movements
so well that we can even stylize our kite

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:41.229
sailing videos with it, where there is tons
of tiny water droplets flying about.

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:42.710
No problems at all.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:48.179
We can also draw on this dog, and remember,
we mentioned that it understands the difference

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:55.409
between foreground and background, and…look,
the scribble correctly travels behind objects.

00:01:55.409 --> 00:02:01.959
Aha, and this is also the reason why we can
easily remove a speeding motorbike from this

00:02:01.959 --> 00:02:03.630
security footage.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.149
Just cut out the foreground layer.

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.149
Nothing to see here.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:11.689
But I wonder, can we go a little more extreme
here?

00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:17.549
And it turns out, these are really nothing
compared to what this new AI can pull off.

00:02:17.549 --> 00:02:18.549
Look.

00:02:18.549 --> 00:02:24.470
We can not only decorate this swan, but, here
is the key…and…oh yes!

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:30.900
The swan is fine, yes, but the reflection
of the swan is also computed correctly.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:36.620
Now this feels like black magic, and we are
not even done yet, now hold on to your papers,

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.159
because here come my two favorite examples!

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.790
Example number one.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.640
Biking in wonderland.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.739
I love this.

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:50.989
Now, you see that not even this technique
is perfect, if you look behind the spokes

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.310
of the wheel, you see a fair amount of warping.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:58.709
I still think this is a miracle that it can
be pulled off at all.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:01.730
Example number two, a picturesque trip.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:07.640
Here, not only the background has been changed,
but even the water has changed as chunks of

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.019
ice have also been added.

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:13.489
And with that, I wonder how easy it is to
do this?

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:18.010
I’ll tell you in a moment, after we look
at this.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.010
Yes.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.220
There is also one issue here with the warping
of the water in the wake of the boat, but

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:28.670
this is an excellent point for us to invoke
the First Law of Papers, which says, do not

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.690
think of where we are, look at where we will
be two more papers down the line.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.659
So, how much work do we have to put in to
pull all this off?

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:40.189
A day of work maybe?

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:42.079
Nope, not even close!

00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:47.450
If you have been holding on to your papers
so far, now, squeeze that paper, and look

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.450
at this.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:52.690
We can unwrap the background of the footage,
and stylize it as we please.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.769
All this takes is just editing one image.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.249
This goes in, this comes out.

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:00.249
Wow.

00:04:00.249 --> 00:04:07.049
Absolutely anyone can do this, so this is
a huge step in democratizing video stylization

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:27.000
and bringing it to everyone.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:49.190
What 
a time to 

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.090
be alive!

00:04:51.090 --> 00:05:11.650
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

